---
import '../styles/comparison.css';
import {data,buildMatrix,detailsMarkup} from '../lib/comparisonModel.js';
const defaults=['speediance','innodigym','tonal','aeke-s1-pro'];
const initialMatrix=buildMatrix(defaults.map(id=>data.gym.find(p=>p.id===id)));
---
<section id="comparison-app" aria-label="Gym and wearable comparison"><div class="comparison-main">
<section data-page-intro class="hero"><h1 data-page-title>Smart gyms &amp; wearables</h1><p>Features, real costs and my buying picks.</p></section>
<section id="compare"><div role="tablist" aria-label="Compare equipment" class="tabs"><button role="tab" id="tab-gym" data-tab="gym" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel">Gym equipment <b id="gym-count">11</b></button><button role="tab" id="tab-wearables" data-tab="wearables" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" aria-controls="panel">Wearables <b id="wear-count">10</b></button></div>
<div id="panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-gym"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE FULL PICTURE</p><h2>Feature comparison</h2><p id="matrix-intro">Photos, features and ownership costs.</p></div><a class="outline-button" href="#costs">See ownership costs ↓</a></div>
<div class="comparison-topline"><p id="selection-status" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="toggle-picker" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="device-chooser">Change devices <span>＋</span></button></div>
<div class="selector-panel" id="device-chooser" hidden><div class="selector-title"><strong id="lineup-heading">Choose up to four devices</strong><button id="reset-picks" class="text-button">Reset picks</button></div><p class="picker-hint">Tap a selected device to remove it, then add another. Photos show the device; the package below states what is included.</p><div class="product-picker" id="product-picker" role="group" aria-label="Choose products to compare"></div></div>
<div class="mobile-selectors"><label>Compare<select id="mobile-a" aria-label="First product"></select></label><span>vs.</span><label>With<select id="mobile-b" aria-label="Second product"></select></label></div>
<div class="matrix-tools"><div class="row-filters" id="row-filters" role="group" aria-label="Feature groups"></div><label class="differences"><input type="checkbox" id="differences"> Only differences</label></div>
<div class="matrix-wrap" id="matrix-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Side-by-side feature comparison"><table id="feature-matrix"><caption class="sr-only">Detailed product features and ownership costs</caption><thead id="matrix-head" set:html={initialMatrix.head}></thead><tbody id="matrix-body" set:html={initialMatrix.body}></tbody></table></div>
<div class="matrix-notes"><span><b>✓</b> Included · Recommendation colors reflect Toby’s buying opinion</span><span>USD · Exact bundles shown in column headers · Sources and qualifications under each product</span></div><div class="cost-disclosure"><b>How costs are calculated</b><p id="cost-disclosure"></p></div>
<section id="costs" class="costs"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE NUMBERS OVER TIME</p><h2>Long-term cost analysis</h2><p>Hardware and required setup, plus the selected level of ongoing service.</p></div><div class="period" role="group" aria-label="Cost chart period"><button data-years="1" aria-pressed="false">1 year</button><button data-years="3" aria-pressed="false">3 years</button><button data-years="5" aria-pressed="true">5 years</button></div></div><div id="verdict-legend" class="verdict-legend"><span class="verdict green">Green · Recommended / specialist fit</span><span class="verdict yellow">Yellow · Consider the tradeoffs</span><span class="verdict red">Red · I would not buy / unavailable</span></div><div id="amp-analysis"></div><div id="rack-analysis"></div><div class="cost-grid"><div class="cost-chart" id="cost-chart"></div><aside class="cost-assumptions"><h3>Make the comparison fair.</h3><p>Compare a usable package, not a deposit or a naked machine. Optional services are listed separately from the default totals.</p><div class="chart-legend"><span><i></i>Hardware & setup</span><span><i></i>Recurring service</span></div><div id="baseline"><label>Traditional gym / month <span class="money-input">$<input type="number" id="gym-monthly" min="0" max="5000" step="1" value="150"></span></label><label>Joining fee <span class="money-input">$<input type="number" id="gym-joining" min="0" max="10000" step="1" value="0"></span></label><div class="gym-total"><span id="gym-period">5-year gym membership</span><strong id="gym-total">$9,000</strong></div><small>Editable baseline from the original page. Your local gym may cost more or less. No commute cost included.</small></div><div id="wear-plan-note" hidden><h4>Required vs. optional</h4><p>WHOOP is a membership with hardware included. Fitbit, Garmin and the other devices have different core and optional tiers; the matrix names the tier being priced.</p></div></aside></div></section>
<section id="ownership"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT IT IS LIKE TO LIVE WITH</p><h2>Pros, cons & buying context</h2><p>Detailed specifications are useful. So are the limitations and the source of each opinion.</p></div></div><div id="product-details" class="product-details" set:html={detailsMarkup("gym")}></div></section>
<div class="comparison-evidence"><div class="experience-pills"><span><i></i>9M+ lbs on Tonal</span><span><i></i>1.29M+ lbs across Speediance machines</span><span><i></i>Ownership history + manufacturer specifications</span></div><small>Training totals retained from the original comparison; they are historical, not live counters.</small></div><section class="method"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE BASIS FOR THE COMPARISON</p><h3>Experience where I have it.<br>Sources where I don’t.</h3></div><div><h4>Personal experience is labeled.</h4><p>My original Tonal history is not a Tonal 2 ownership test. Joel’s AEKE K1 interview is his experience. New models are compared using their published specifications.</p></div><div><h4>Prices have a defined scope.</h4><p>The date, exact product configuration, required service and excluded costs are listed. Promotions can change. Manufacturer claims are not independent lab measurements.</p></div></section></div></section><div id="toast" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
</div></section>
<script>
 import {initComparison} from '../lib/comparisonClient.js';
 initComparison();
 document.addEventListener('astro:page-load',initComparison);
</script>
